<title>BELGIUM: KREDIETBANK RISE MYSTIFIES TRADERS.</title>
<headline>KREDIETBANK RISE MYSTIFIES TRADERS.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Belgian bank Kredietbank jumped more than six percent on Thursday and dealers said they were surprised at the sharp rise.</p>
<p>Kredietbank closed up 6.14 percent at 12,100 francs after earlier touching a new record high of 12,400 francs, up more than seven percent.</p>
<p>&quot;Everybody agrees that Kredietbank had lagged the rest of the banks in Belgium, but I'm surprised by the sharp rise,&quot; said analyst Patrick Millecam at brokerage Coluy &amp; Co.</p>
<p>Dealers said one reason for the rise may have been a positive article in the Wall Street Journal Europe newspaper.</p>
<p>-- Paul de Bendern, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6817, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
